WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.027 --> 00:00:02.050
- [Announcer] Thanks to
Wix for keeping Legal Eagle

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.341
in the air and our website on the web.

00:00:04.341 --> 00:00:05.810
- (laughs) I don't believe it.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.720
You're meant to come
down here and defend me

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.420
against these characters
and the only one I've got

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.020
on my side is the blood-sucking lawyer.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.573
- I take offense at that.

00:00:13.573 --> 00:00:17.280
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.560
Hey Legal Eagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.200
Welcome back to Laws Broken,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.874
where an attorney destroys
your favorite childhood movies

00:00:24.874 --> 00:00:28.470
by showing you how illegal everything is,

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.730
because everything is illegal.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.330
- Hold on to your butts.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:34.510
- This week we're going
to examine Jurassic Park.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.820
As Ian Malcolm would
say, it's like Disneyland

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.000
if the Pirates of the
Caribbean ate all the tourists.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.470
There will be negligence.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.530
Be sure to subscribe and comment

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.020
in the form of an objection,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.340
which I will either sustain or overrule,

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.920
and stick around until
the end of the video

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.530
where I give a verdict for John
Hammond's civil liabilities

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.118
and how long Dennis
Nedry would go to jail.

00:00:56.118 --> 00:00:57.930
- Huh, we spared no expense.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.190
Spared no expense.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.430
Spared no expense.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.879
- The bottom line is that
expenses were spared.

00:01:03.879 --> 00:01:05.439
(dramatic music)
(zapping)

00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:07.910
(roars)

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.793
Let's examine the evidence.

00:01:09.793 --> 00:01:14.793
(tense music)
(dinosaur growling)

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:25.870
Okay, starting off with a bang here.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.290
I am pretty confident
that OSHA regulations

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:32.230
do not permit you to
have a loaded shotgun,

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:36.260
as well as dozens of men
surrounded with cattle prods.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.620
That seems like a very
dangerous working condition

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.480
that probably violates a number
of health and safety codes.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.236
This is clearly an unsafe
working environment

00:01:45.236 --> 00:01:47.440
that is going to lead to numerous

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.340
on-the-job accidents and injuries.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.625
Of course, at least they
are wearing hard hats,

00:01:51.625 --> 00:01:54.739
which would make sense if
this were a construction site,

00:01:54.739 --> 00:01:57.040
but this is more like a zoo,

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.550
so I think those particular hard hats,

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.750
in addition to not making
sense in this context,

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.690
probably make things more dangerous

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.100
given that they're not
going to do anything

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.890
to protect themselves
from the velociraptors.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.930
So their head's in the right spot,

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.160
but they have no idea what they're doing,

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.260
and they are certainly not OSHA complaint.

00:02:17.513 --> 00:02:20.030
(growling)

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.273
- Push 10 more in there.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:24.440
- But at least unlike Willy Wonka,

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.710
at least they were smart enough to put

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:29.091
OSHA compliant handrails
on their buildings.

00:02:29.091 --> 00:02:30.460
- And push.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.460
(tense music)
(door creaking)

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.610
We're off, loading team step away.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.970
- So in addition to shotguns and tasers,

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:47.790
a lot of these men are
armed with automatic M16s.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.700
I kinda doubt there are
any zoos in the world

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.909
that equip their zookeepers
with cattle prods

00:02:52.909 --> 00:02:57.120
and automatic weapons, that
seems counterproductive.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.797
- Raise the gate.

00:02:58.797 --> 00:03:01.297
(tense music)

00:03:08.052 --> 00:03:10.885
(dinosaur growls)

00:03:11.871 --> 00:03:14.593
- So that seems like a
terribly designed system.

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:16.486
(yells)

00:03:16.486 --> 00:03:18.556
- Lock the openings,
don't let them get out.

00:03:18.556 --> 00:03:20.723
(yelling)

00:03:24.093 --> 00:03:27.280
- I'm sorry, I shouldn't
laugh at this carnage.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.350
Okay so there are a lot of problems here.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.720
First of all, whoever designed this system

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.989
did a terrible job because
simply by the raptors

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:37.950
running out of the cage it was
able to push everything back

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.810
and grab one of these poor workers.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.210
I think there is a clear
products liability problem

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.200
with whoever designed
this entrapment system,

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.834
and on top of it, the person
that put this park together

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.780
I think has some major negligence issues,

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.110
which will be a running
theme throughout this video.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:56.400
This thing easily could have
been designed in such a way

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.124
to prevent the cage from
moving back away from the wall

00:04:00.124 --> 00:04:03.340
and keeping all of these individuals safe.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.580
Just make it all automated
and use mechanics

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.240
and hydraulics instead
of requiring a human

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:11.110
to open and close this cage
and stand on top of it.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.980
This kind of foreseeable injury is exactly

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.900
what negligence is made
to protect against,

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.313
and this is a bad system.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:19.453
- 750.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:22.700
On delivery, 50,000 more
for each viable embryo,

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.040
that's 1.5 million if you get
all 15 species off the island.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.020
- Oh I'll get them all.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.710
- Remember, viable embryos.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.170
They're no use to us
if they don't survive.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.413
- Oh, how am I supposed to transport them?

00:04:36.827 --> 00:04:38.516
- The bottom screws open.

00:04:38.516 --> 00:04:41.179
- (laughs) That's great.

00:04:41.179 --> 00:04:42.020
Look at that.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.905
- It's cooled and compartmentalized.

00:04:44.905 --> 00:04:45.993
- You got us one, that's great.

00:04:45.993 --> 00:04:48.276
- Customs can even check
it if they want to.

00:04:48.276 --> 00:04:49.859
- Let me see.
- Go on.

00:04:49.859 --> 00:04:50.810
- Oh.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.690
- There's enough coolant
inside for 36 hours.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:53.890
- No menthol?

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:57.020
- The embryos have to be back
here in San Jose by then.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.610
- That's up to your guy on the boat.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.450
Seven o'clock tomorrow
night on the east dock.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:01.910
Make sure he gets it right.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:05.560
- All right, what we have
here is a civil and criminal

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:08.570
conspiracy between these
two individuals to engage in

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.640
a number of different
crimes and business torts.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.370
What Dodgson and Nedry are doing here is

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.950
they are conspiring to
steal the trade secrets

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.970
of Hammond and Ingen, which constitutes

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.300
the criminal act of theft,

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.600
and it also constitutes the
civil wrong of conversion.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:30.240
Conversion is the civil version of theft.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.200
So they're trying to steal
these dinosaur embryos

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.860
from Jurassic Park.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.530
Now, given then Dodgson is
paying Nedry millions of dollars

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:41.392
to engage in this theft
and this conspiracy,

00:05:41.392 --> 00:05:44.910
we can reasonably say that
the value of the things

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.271
that Nedry is stealing are worth at least

00:05:47.271 --> 00:05:49.670
as much as he's getting paid, so millions

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.770
if not tens of millions of dollars.

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:53.790
Given the dollar amounts at issue,

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:58.364
this theft gets enhanced into
the felony of grand larceny,

00:05:58.364 --> 00:06:02.691
which carries with it easily
five to 20 years in jail,

00:06:02.691 --> 00:06:04.480
depending on the circumstances.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.790
On top of that, they are
engaging in a civil conspiracy

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:10.350
to steal trade secrets,
which carries with it

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.900
a hefty civil fine along with it.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.150
So that is just the
beginning of the crimes

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:17.940
that both of those guys are
gonna be on the hook for.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.840
- I'll tell you the problem
with the scientific power

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:21.530
that you're using here.

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.933
It didn't require any
discipline to attain it.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:27.370
You know, you read what others had done,

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.130
and you took the next step.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.630
You didn't earn the
knowledge for yourselves,

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:34.385
so you don't take any
responsibility for it.

00:06:34.385 --> 00:06:36.610
You stood on the shoulders of geniuses

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.030
to accomplish something
as fast as you could,

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.770
and before you even knew what you had,

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:43.290
you patented it and packaged it

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.130
and slapped it on a plastic lunchbox,

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.828
and now you're selling it.
(banging)

00:06:46.828 --> 00:06:48.553
You want to sell it, well.

00:06:48.553 --> 00:06:51.470
- I don't think you're
giving us our due credit.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:52.920
Our scientists have done things

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.760
which nobody has ever done before.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.010
- Yeah, yeah but your
scientists were so preoccupied

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:58.240
with whether or not they
could that they didn't

00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:59.850
stop to think if they should.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.830
- So Malcolm raises a
really interesting point.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:06.673
The dinosaurs in this park
are not naturally occurring

00:07:06.673 --> 00:07:08.890
animals like you would find in a zoo.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:12.040
These are essentially
products that they created.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.780
When you put a product,
whether it is a car

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:18.583
or a pharmaceutical drug
into the stream of commerce,

00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:22.080
you are often responsible for the damages

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.250
that occur as a result
of that particular use.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.540
And in Jurassic Park, the
products are the dinosaurs.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:33.010
They have packaged it into a
theme park-like environment,

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.400
but if a drug needs to
carry with it a warning

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.240
that there are side
effects, you can imagine

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:41.630
what kind of warnings would be necessary

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:45.680
for a Tyrannosaurus
Rex or any of the other

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:48.355
dinosaurs on this island.

00:07:48.355 --> 00:07:49.910
- (scoffs) I don't believe it.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:51.610
You're meant to come
down here and defend me

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.200
against these characters
and the only one I've got

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.910
on my side is the blood-sucking lawyer.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.160
- I take offense at that.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:01.080
- National Weather Service
is tracking a tropical storm

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.200
about 75 miles west of us.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.060
- Ay ay ay ay, why didn't
I build in Orlando?

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:06.893
- I'll keep an eye on it,

00:08:06.893 --> 00:08:09.700
maybe it will swing
south like the last one.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.992
- So a tropical storm is
going to hit Jurassic Park.

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:15.880
This could actually cut in
two different ways here.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:18.220
On the one hand, if you build a theme park

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:21.675
off the coast of Costa
Rica, you should expect to

00:08:21.675 --> 00:08:24.620
deal with hurricanes
every once in a while.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.370
On the other hand, there
is a concept in law

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:30.300
called force majeure, which
is basically an act of god

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:33.120
which is so unforeseeable
that no one can really

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.680
be held responsible,
so you might argue that

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.160
this particular hurricane
might be so severe

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:40.610
and so unusual that there's no way

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:41.970
Hammond could have planned for it

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.240
and that he is not responsible
for the things that go wrong

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.552
as a result of this particular
tropical storm or hurricane.

00:08:47.552 --> 00:08:50.299
So those are the two
ways that it could go.

00:08:50.299 --> 00:08:52.550
I'm not sure which way it comes out

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.648
in this particular case, we'll see.

00:08:54.648 --> 00:08:57.930
- Oh uh, I finished debugging the phones.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.150
You know, I was gonna debug, so I did.

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:02.000
You know, you told me to
get started on debugging

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.750
the phone and I thought
maybe I should tell you

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:08.470
that the system's gonna be
compiling for 18 to 20 minutes,

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:10.560
so some of the minor systems,
they might go on and off

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:11.840
for a while, but it's
nothing to worry about,

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.933
it's a simple thing.
(tense music)

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:22.780
- All right, so Nedry has engaged in

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.500
probably what constitutes a number of

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.370
different computer and hacking crimes.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.690
He has clearly exceeded his authorization

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:32.390
regarding the Jurassic
Park computer network.

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:35.520
He is using it for his
own nefarious purposes,

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:37.770
and not only that, but
he's endangering the lives

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:41.390
of everyone on this tour,
but because he has exceeded

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.370
his authorization for the network,

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.850
he's essentially trespassing

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.500
to all of the different
computers and the locks

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:51.020
and electronic systems on Jurassic Park.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:54.160
He's also engaged in
computer fraud basically,

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.010
by using a computer for
fraudulent purposes.

00:09:57.010 --> 00:10:00.870
On top of that, the
hacking itself is part of

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:04.370
his scheme to steal the trade secrets

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:08.860
and the biological embryos
from Jurassic Park,

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.239
so it's part of this larger conspiracy

00:10:11.239 --> 00:10:13.920
to commit grand larceny.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.350
So now would probably be a good time

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:17.100
to tell you about the felony murder rule,

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.660
because I think it's going to be relevant

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.260
in this particular context.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.140
The felony murder rule
states that if you commit

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.880
an inherently dangerous
felony and during the course

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.710
of thing felony someone is killed,

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:31.120
you are on the hook for
first degree murder,

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:33.680
which is the worst kind of
murder that the law recognizes.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:35.600
It's essentially the premeditated killing.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.070
It's like an assassination,

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.276
you intended to kill
the particular victim.

00:10:40.276 --> 00:10:43.976
The felony murder rule is an
exception to the general rule

00:10:43.976 --> 00:10:46.510
that to commit first degree murder,

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.270
you have to have that mens rea,

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:50.720
that intentionality of
killing that person.

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:53.590
And often, that is how
you get the death penalty

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.720
in states that still
have the death penalty.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.060
So if I was a prosecutor and
I was trying to prosecute

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:00.412
Nedry to the maximum extent possible,

00:11:00.412 --> 00:11:03.060
I would argue that theft,
in this particular case

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:06.837
grand larceny and conspiracy
to commit grand larceny,

00:11:06.837 --> 00:11:09.610
are one of the things that
qualify as being inherently

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:11.670
dangerous, and Nedry might be on the hook

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.440
for the first degree murder of the people

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.940
that die during the course
of his attempted theft.

00:11:17.019 --> 00:11:19.352
(crunching)

00:11:24.319 --> 00:11:29.319
- Oh Jesus, oh Jesus.

00:11:30.419 --> 00:11:33.560
- He left us, he left us.

00:11:34.827 --> 00:11:39.636
(thunder cracks)
(breathing heavily)

00:11:39.636 --> 00:11:40.469
- I don't feel like this is

00:11:40.469 --> 00:11:42.293
an accurate portrayal of attorneys.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.080
- Where does he think he's going?

00:11:46.319 --> 00:11:48.963
- When you gotta go, you gotta go.

00:11:48.963 --> 00:11:51.796
(dinosaur stomps)

00:11:53.565 --> 00:11:56.315
(metal creaking)

00:12:00.562 --> 00:12:03.312
(thunder cracks)

00:12:05.892 --> 00:12:06.892
- Dr. Grant?

00:12:08.155 --> 00:12:10.322
(roaring)

00:12:16.693 --> 00:12:20.540
- All right, so the T-Rex
has broken out of its paddock

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.540
because the electricity went down

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:25.950
and the fence is no longer electrified.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:29.130
To me, this situation scream negligence.

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:30.560
Negligence is one of the first things

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:31.880
you learn about in law school.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:34.940
To prove negligence,
you have to show a duty

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.680
between one person and another,

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:38.170
you have to have a breach of that duty,

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:39.850
you have to have a causation between

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:42.177
the breach of that duty
and the damages suffered,

00:12:42.177 --> 00:12:45.100
and you have to have actual damages.

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:47.430
Duty is important because strangers

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.260
don't owe each other anything.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.460
The classic example is if you saw someone

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:53.560
drowning in a pool, you don't have

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:56.630
an affirmative obligation
to help that person.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:59.070
You probably should, but legally speaking,

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:01.370
you generally don't have
a requirement to do so

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:06.190
unless there is some obligation
to affirmatively act.

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:09.100
That's what a duty is, and
when you create a theme park,

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:12.140
you have a duty to your tourists,

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.130
the people that are in that park.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:16.460
Whether you have breached
your duty depends on

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.781
whether you have upheld the standards

00:13:18.781 --> 00:13:20.830
of someone else in your position.

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:23.160
In other words, what would a reasonable

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.860
proprietor of a theme park do?

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:28.986
Did the damages, the harm
that someone incurred,

00:13:28.986 --> 00:13:31.940
did that result from
the foreseeable results

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:33.360
of someone's actions?

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:36.140
So looking at it in
this particular context,

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:39.400
we have a Tyrannosaurus Rex in a paddock.

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:40.920
They have taken precautions to make sure

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.200
that the T-Rex doesn't get out.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:46.060
They have put an electrified
fence containing this T-Rex,

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:47.998
and when that fence is electrified,

00:13:47.998 --> 00:13:50.820
the T-Rex doesn't get out,
it knows that it's going to

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.920
get shocked and the shocks
are enough to keep it inside.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:57.530
However, can we expect things to go wrong?

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:01.200
Is it foreseeable that the fence might not

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.400
be electrified at all times?

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.470
I would say yes, 100%.

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:08.387
So what should you do as the proprietor of

00:14:08.387 --> 00:14:10.017
a dinosaur theme park?

00:14:10.017 --> 00:14:12.812
Well, you should take
precautions to make sure

00:14:12.812 --> 00:14:15.160
that if the electricity goes down,

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.840
the T-Rex still can't get out.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:20.030
What that means in practice
is maybe a second fence,

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:24.030
one that is able to withstand
the might of the T-Rex.

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:26.890
It seems like the T-Rex here
was able to put its mass in

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:31.055
or use its tiny arm
claws to be able to snap

00:14:31.055 --> 00:14:33.980
the steel cables here, which
means that they could have

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:37.370
used a fence with stronger steel cables.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:39.860
Separately, maybe you
have a backup generator

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:43.329
that goes into effect
immediately when the first line

00:14:43.329 --> 00:14:45.800
of electricity goes down,
that's a different way

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:47.200
that you can solve this problem.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.270
A third way to prevent
this problem would be

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:51.850
to not use a fence at all.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:55.110
I've been to many zoos that
have very large animals

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:58.749
like elephants and giraffes
where those animals are

00:14:58.749 --> 00:15:01.111
far below where the tourists are,

00:15:01.111 --> 00:15:04.720
so the change in elevation is big enough

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:07.550
that there's no way for the
animal to get to the high ground

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.440
where all the people are.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:11.830
So the natural barriers,
the difference in elevation

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:15.534
is enough to keep the
animals from attacking

00:15:15.534 --> 00:15:18.070
the tourists and the sightseers.

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:19.791
So those are three different ways

00:15:19.791 --> 00:15:22.120
that the designers of Jurassic Park

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.540
could have designed this
particular enclosure

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.030
to keep the tourists safe,

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:27.860
and there's really no question that

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:30.080
this negligence resulted in the injuries

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:31.090
that these people are going to suffer.

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:33.320
The emotional distress
and the physical injuries

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.180
that they're going to
suffer are a direct result

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:38.480
of the T-Rex getting out, so
there's a direct causal link,

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.350
what's called proximate
cause under the law

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:44.800
between the negligence in
question and their injuries.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:47.330
So this is a slam dunk case, I think,

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:50.481
against Jurassic Park for pure negligence,

00:15:50.481 --> 00:15:52.657
bordering on recklessness

00:15:52.657 --> 00:15:55.738
for these poor people in these cars.

00:15:55.738 --> 00:16:00.738
(breathing heavily)
(dinosaur screeches)

00:16:01.181 --> 00:16:04.407
- Oh, hi, nice boy, nice boy.

00:16:05.832 --> 00:16:08.260
- So we have the situation where

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:12.350
we have a really bad actor
who is going to suffer

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:14.530
some physical injuries, spoiler alert,

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:17.182
as a result of his own bad acts.

00:16:17.182 --> 00:16:19.380
(groans)
(dinosaur screeches)

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:22.050
But also partially as a result of

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:24.820
some of the negligence of the park owners.

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:27.270
So in this particular
situation, it's possible

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:31.040
that if he were able to sue
as a result of his injuries

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.020
and not being eaten alive by a dinosaur,

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.730
he might be able to get some recovery.

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:39.180
Yes, he was partially responsible,
but in most jurisdictions

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:41.000
they use what's called comparative fault,

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.870
which means that if you are at fault for

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:46.300
a certain bad thing happening to you

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:49.170
and someone else is also
responsible for that thing,

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:51.100
well you just look at
the various percentages

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:53.510
and you say well okay,
if it was a 50/50 split,

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:57.890
then you're entitled to recover
50% of the actual damages.

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:00.470
That is in contrast to
what states used to use,

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:02.230
which is called contributory negligence,

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:05.632
which is that if you're
responsible for even one percent

00:17:05.632 --> 00:17:09.390
of your own damages you're not
entitled to receive anything.

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:11.980
They're are pros and cons
with both situations,

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:15.940
but equity generally is
in favor of comparative

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:19.900
negligence instead, so Nedry
might be able to file suit.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:22.150
However on the other
hand, there is a doctrine

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:24.990
called Unclean Hands
which says that you're not

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:28.038
able to profit from your own bad acts,

00:17:28.038 --> 00:17:30.986
and Nedry's acts are so bad in this case,

00:17:30.986 --> 00:17:33.180
I think he would probably be precluded

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.380
from recovering anything.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.630
(grunting)

00:17:38.792 --> 00:17:40.240
(rattling)

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.292
(dinosaur screeches)

00:17:42.292 --> 00:17:44.200
(yelling)

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:48.900
So Nedry passes away as a
result of his own bad acts,

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:52.040
but interestingly, because
he entered into a conspiracy,

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:54.960
conceivably the other
members of this conspiracy

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:58.070
might be responsible for Nedry's death,

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:00.767
both civilly and criminally as well.

00:18:00.767 --> 00:18:03.898
(upbeat music)

00:18:03.898 --> 00:18:05.160
(dinosaur growls)
- No, no, no!

00:18:12.784 --> 00:18:17.482
(fence clattering)
(dramatic music)

00:18:17.482 --> 00:18:18.710
- Oh, Mr. Arnold.

00:18:24.556 --> 00:18:27.696
(tense music)
(dinosaur snorts)

00:18:27.696 --> 00:18:30.919
- Clever girl.
(dinosaur screeches)

00:18:30.919 --> 00:18:32.919
(yells)

00:18:34.855 --> 00:18:37.855
(sad trombone music)

00:18:37.855 --> 00:18:39.757
- Are you crazy, I'm not gonna jump.

00:18:39.757 --> 00:18:41.098
- You can do it, Dr. Grant says.

00:18:41.098 --> 00:18:44.348
- I'll count to three, one, two, three.

00:18:46.354 --> 00:18:47.187
- 11, 12.

00:18:49.103 --> 00:18:50.607
- I'm coming up, I'm coming up to get you.

00:18:50.607 --> 00:18:51.450
Lex, I gotta get Tim.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:54.153
- Okay, I'm gonna count to three.

00:18:57.022 --> 00:19:00.075
One,
(alarms blare)

00:19:00.075 --> 00:19:02.521
two,
(zapping)

00:19:02.521 --> 00:19:04.104
- Oh boy.

00:19:04.104 --> 00:19:06.805
All right, now just as it is foreseeable

00:19:06.805 --> 00:19:09.540
that the electricity's going to go down

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.040
on these electrified fences,

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.910
it's also foreseeable that
a human might be able to

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:17.510
touch these fences as well,
so not only do you need

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:19.650
the electric fence to
keep the dinosaurs in,

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:22.505
but you also have to have
a way to keep the humans

00:19:22.505 --> 00:19:25.810
away from this electrified fence as well.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:28.530
Yet another reason why
these electrified fences

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:31.410
were just a bad, bad
idea in the first place.

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:33.020
The question is, is it foreseeable

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:35.400
that a human would ever
touch these fences?

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.890
Well, as we saw from
earlier in this movie,

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:40.210
it was incredibly easy for the characters

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:42.730
to leave the cars when they wanted to.

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:45.786
(doors closing)

00:19:45.786 --> 00:19:46.980
(growls)

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:50.090
One precaution you could
take is to make it so that

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:53.730
no one can leave the cars
as they're taking the tour.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.600
That might open up a whole
bunch of other problems,

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:57.470
but at least it would prevent people from

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:59.037
touching the fence here.

00:19:59.037 --> 00:20:01.790
In this particular iteration,
we see that it's very easy

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:04.150
for people to leave and
there is nothing preventing

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:07.304
these people from touching
these electrified fences.

00:20:07.304 --> 00:20:09.789
So I think it is incredibly foreseeable

00:20:09.789 --> 00:20:13.740
that someone, some
person might accidentally

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:16.050
touch the electrified fence and be shocked

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:17.879
in the same way that Tim was here.

00:20:17.879 --> 00:20:22.879
(tense music)
(bones clattering)

00:20:24.135 --> 00:20:29.135
(groaning)
(dinosaur growls)

00:20:29.247 --> 00:20:31.936
- [Grant] Tim, let go, yes.

00:20:31.936 --> 00:20:33.936
(yells)

00:20:36.409 --> 00:20:39.670
- Okay, I suppose this is a
minor thing in the context

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.180
of an island full of
dinosaurs killing people,

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:45.390
but those fossils probably weigh thousands

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.700
and thousands of pounds, I
don't think they should be

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:50.700
buckling under the additional
weight of a couple of people,

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:53.408
and the fact that they're
falling apart is yet more

00:20:53.408 --> 00:20:56.564
evidence of negligence
by the park owners here.

00:20:56.564 --> 00:21:01.231
(tense music)
(yelling)

00:21:03.173 --> 00:21:04.420
(bones clatter)

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:07.690
So given the height that those
two characters fell from,

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:10.580
I think we can safely add a sprained ankle

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:14.144
and perhaps a broken foot
to the pain and suffering

00:21:14.144 --> 00:21:18.611
and medical bills that Jurassic
Park is responsible for.

00:21:18.611 --> 00:21:20.340
- That is one big pile of (bleep).

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:22.880
- All right, welcome to Jurassic Park.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.440
Jurassic Park.

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:26.178
Let's tally up the crimes.

00:21:26.178 --> 00:21:28.090
(dramatic music)

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:30.380
Here the main bad actor is Nedry.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:32.650
He engaged in multiple criminal acts.

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:37.650
First he attempted to steal
trade secrets from the company.

00:21:37.825 --> 00:21:39.440
Given the value of the larceny,

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.630
I would peg his sentence at 20 years.

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:45.620
On top of that, during the
commission of this felony

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:48.500
that was inherently
dangerous, three people died,

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:51.940
including Muldoon, Arnold, and the lawyer.

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:54.600
- People are dying.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:57.650
- Given the felony murder
rule, Nedry would be guilty

00:21:57.650 --> 00:22:00.700
of three counts of first degree murder,

00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:03.900
the worst kind of murder,
and he would certainly

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:05.530
be sent to jail for the rest of his life,

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:08.740
if not put on death
row, effectively serving

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:11.662
three back-to-back life sentences.

00:22:11.662 --> 00:22:14.245
(upbeat music)

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:18.950
Regarding John Hammond as
the owner of Jurassic Park,

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:21.480
I don't think he would
be criminally liable.

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:24.320
He clearly didn't intend
for any of this to happen,

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:26.913
so he lacked the mens rea
for most criminal acts.

00:22:26.913 --> 00:22:28.260
With that being said,

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:31.281
their gross negligence
is clearly apparent.

00:22:31.281 --> 00:22:34.390
Skimping out on dinosaur-proof fences

00:22:34.390 --> 00:22:35.994
and not creating a back-up system

00:22:35.994 --> 00:22:38.530
for when those fences
were no longer electrified

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:41.760
is clearly an act of
negligence, and they are

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:44.740
responsible for the civil
damages that occurred.

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:47.630
Included in that are
probably the wrongful deaths

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:49.300
of the three people
that died, which include

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:52.770
Muldoon, Arnold, and the lawyer as well,

00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:55.510
not to mention the OSHA
violations at the beginning

00:22:55.510 --> 00:22:58.950
of the movie which led
to the poor park worker

00:22:58.950 --> 00:23:00.690
being eaten alive by a raptor,

00:23:00.690 --> 00:23:03.670
so that's four counts of wrongful death.

00:23:03.670 --> 00:23:06.590
How much a jury would
award would depend largely

00:23:06.590 --> 00:23:09.280
on their lifetime earning
capacity, but let's

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:12.510
conservatively say five
million dollars per person.

00:23:12.510 --> 00:23:14.780
On top of that, there is
the pain and suffering

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:17.000
and medical bills for
all of the other people

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:20.144
that went to the park
under false pretenses.

00:23:20.144 --> 00:23:23.810
(fence clatters)
(cries)

00:23:23.810 --> 00:23:27.670
So let's peg that at about a
million dollars per person.

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:30.690
So add it all together,
that is $25 million

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:33.980
that Jurassic Park owes
to the surviving members

00:23:33.980 --> 00:23:36.950
of the excursion, and the
family members of those that

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:39.750
didn't quite make it all the
way through Jurassic Park.

00:23:39.750 --> 00:23:42.670
- After careful
consideration, I've decided

00:23:42.670 --> 00:23:45.070
not to endorse your park.

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:45.950
- Damn.

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:48.100
- Now if you're going to
start a dinosaur theme park

00:23:48.100 --> 00:23:50.430
that may or may not
kill all of its patrons,

00:23:50.430 --> 00:23:52.360
you're going to need a
website to advertise it.

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:54.710
When I needed a website for
helping law school students,

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:57.160
which for the record
contains no dinosaurs,

